1
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:12,470
You still don't know
Satoko's whereabouts?

2
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:15,598
No. It seems the investigation
isn't going well, either.

3
00:00:16,975 --> 00:00:20,185
{\an8}Satoko...
Where on earth have you gone?

4
00:00:20,186 --> 00:00:21,186
Master.

5
00:00:21,187 --> 00:00:22,229
Hm?

6
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:23,857
You have a guest.

7
00:00:24,357 --> 00:00:25,567
Pardon me.

8
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:27,526
And who might you be?

9
00:00:27,527 --> 00:00:30,530
My name is Eishin Nitobe.

10
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:35,618
I've come to deliver a message
from Miss Satoko.

11
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:43,292
What?!

12
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:45,086
You're leaving the island tonight?!

13
00:00:46,463 --> 00:00:50,340
This is so sudden.
How are you even going to manage that?

14
00:00:50,341 --> 00:00:53,010
We've bribed the boatman.

15
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:56,097
There's a reason I have to
leave the island in such a hurry.

16
00:00:56,973 --> 00:00:58,558
You'll come back, right?

17
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:08,692
I've had so much fun working here
these past five days since you saved me.

18
00:01:08,693 --> 00:01:10,736
I'm also grateful that
Yukari and the others

19
00:01:10,737 --> 00:01:12,489
have changed
their attitude toward me.

20
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:15,658
We'll always be friends, right?

21
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:17,911
Yes!

22
00:01:19,579 --> 00:01:21,706
We'll always be friends!

23
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:25,251
I'm glad.

24
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:42,101
<i>Time really flew by.</i>

25
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:45,772
<i>It was a short time,</i>

26
00:01:46,397 --> 00:01:48,066
<i>but I'm truly grateful to you.</i>

27
00:02:06,417 --> 00:02:08,252
<i>Sticky and clinging</i>

28
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:11,214
<i>I take off the lint</i>

29
00:02:12,132 --> 00:02:13,757
{\an8}<i>To the way wind blows</i>

30
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:16,928
{\an8}<i>I quit walking like that</i>

31
00:02:17,846 --> 00:02:20,264
<i>Bashful but rejecting heart</i>

32
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:22,099
<i>If it's me</i>

33
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:24,977
<i>It's faster when the
awoken morning comes</i>

34
00:02:24,978 --> 00:02:27,980
<i>I breathe, distant tomorrow</i>

35
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:29,022
<i>It's yours</i>

36
00:02:29,023 --> 00:02:31,400
<i>Simplified and pathetic,</i>

37
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:33,861
<i>Can you turn off those festival lights?</i>

38
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:35,237
<i>Even in the dark</i>

39
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:37,322
<i>If we look for each other</i>

40
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:39,951
<i>They glow, our tears</i>

41
00:02:40,285 --> 00:02:42,327
<i>It feels like we are struggling</i>

42
00:02:42,328 --> 00:02:45,372
<i>But we're moving on no matter where</i>

43
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:47,916
{\an8}<i>So absorbed, I was about to stop</i>

44
00:02:47,917 --> 00:02:51,253
<i>The days I left behind</i>

45
00:02:51,254 --> 00:02:53,130
<i>They made me bloom</i>

46
00:02:53,131 --> 00:02:55,632
<i>The last moments on my own</i>

47
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:58,552
<i>With simple and plain things</i>

48
00:02:58,553 --> 00:02:59,511
<i>I want to live</i>

49
00:02:59,512 --> 00:03:01,513
<i>No one else's "now"</i>

50
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:04,349
<i>Set it to the sound raining down</i>

51
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:06,810
{\an8}<i>Slip through the streets</i>

52
00:03:06,811 --> 00:03:09,855
{\an8}<i>Drenched in untouchable love</i>

53
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:12,774
<i>I can be me because</i>

54
00:03:12,775 --> 00:03:15,652
<i>You are who you are</i>

55
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:16,486
<i>/ various</i>

56
00:03:16,487 --> 00:03:18,488
<i>The days I appended</i>

57
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:19,448
<i>/ various</i>

58
00:03:19,449 --> 00:03:21,241
<i>The genuine period</i>

59
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:22,242
<i>/ various</i>

60
00:03:22,243 --> 00:03:24,202
<i>What few days I added</i>

61
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:27,456
{\an8}<i>Shifted, the period can still be away</i>

62
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:30,000
(Firefly Wedding)

63
00:03:30,001 --> 00:03:36,674
(The Demon and the Heart)

64
00:03:41,429 --> 00:03:44,556
How long will it take us
to reach the other side?

65
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:47,559
Hmm...
About four or five hours, I guess.

66
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:50,647
Wow. That's quite a long time.

67
00:03:51,356 --> 00:03:54,150
So we'll arrive around dawn, huh?

68
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:55,818
It seems so.

69
00:03:58,571 --> 00:04:03,575
<i>This is so awkward! This silence...
I have to say something.</i>

70
00:04:03,576 --> 00:04:06,828
<i>But what should I talk about?</i>

71
00:04:06,829 --> 00:04:09,456
<i>After all,
this man and I are going to...</i>

72
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:14,419
<i>He said he would kidnap me
once we reached the mainland.</i>

73
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:16,381
<i>Is he serious about that?</i>

74
00:04:20,134 --> 00:04:23,095
<i>He's acting strange, too.</i>

75
00:04:23,096 --> 00:04:25,889
<i>I've never really understood
what goes on in his head,</i>

76
00:04:25,890 --> 00:04:28,101
<i>but he's especially strange today...</i>

77
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:32,896
<i>Anyway, I don't want to lie to him or
hide anything from him anymore.</i>

78
00:04:32,897 --> 00:04:33,897
Um...

79
00:04:33,898 --> 00:04:34,898
Hm?

80
00:04:34,899 --> 00:04:39,027
I've been thinking...
Could you take me to the Kirigaya house?

81
00:04:39,028 --> 00:04:41,781
I'd like to repay you properly.

82
00:04:42,615 --> 00:04:44,784
I can't marry you, but...

83
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:47,327
I don't think it's right

84
00:04:47,328 --> 00:04:51,207
to simply brush you off
and run away as soon as we arrive.

85
00:04:52,834 --> 00:04:55,753
I want to marry you, Satoko.

86
00:04:56,921 --> 00:05:00,924
But you want to go home,

87
00:05:00,925 --> 00:05:03,844
and I don't think it's right
for me to stop you.

88
00:05:03,845 --> 00:05:07,724
I've been wondering what to do
once we get there.

89
00:05:08,474 --> 00:05:10,767
I love you, Satoko,

90
00:05:10,768 --> 00:05:14,188
so I don't want you to be unhappy.

91
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:20,819
So that's why things have been
so awkward between us.

92
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:22,571
Awkward?

93
00:05:22,572 --> 00:05:24,406
Was I being awkward?

94
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:27,659
But we still have to decide what to do.

95
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:28,661
Hmm?

96
00:05:30,204 --> 00:05:34,792
I'm sorry, but I can't back down.

97
00:05:36,961 --> 00:05:38,170
Neither can I.

98
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:42,674
Even if marrying me
won't make you happy,

99
00:05:42,675 --> 00:05:46,845
I still want to marry you,
no matter what happens.

100
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:48,556
I don't care what anyone else thinks.

101
00:05:50,266 --> 00:05:54,144
Then become someone of sufficient status
to convince my father to accept you.

102
00:05:54,145 --> 00:05:57,148
Huh?
Can I still become someone like that?

103
00:05:57,648 --> 00:05:58,940
That might be difficult.

104
00:05:58,941 --> 00:06:01,569
Ah, you were teasing me!

105
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:08,617
If we'd met
under different circumstances,

106
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:12,080
we might have gotten to know each other
in a different way, too.

107
00:06:12,830 --> 00:06:16,917
I was afraid of you at first,

108
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:19,879
but now I'm glad I met you.

109
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:26,426
Satoko, you're so mature.

110
00:06:26,427 --> 00:06:28,637
You're always the one calming me down.

111
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:34,560
Being with you is the happiest thing
that's ever happened to me.

112
00:06:54,664 --> 00:06:57,165
Looks like they've found us after all.

113
00:06:57,166 --> 00:06:58,417
What is that?

114
00:06:59,293 --> 00:07:01,170
They're pursuers from the island.

115
00:07:04,632 --> 00:07:07,844
{\an8}Wow, they really look like
they mean business.

116
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:10,554
Satoko, stay down.

117
00:07:10,555 --> 00:07:12,305
I'll go sink a few of their boats.

118
00:07:12,306 --> 00:07:13,181
What?!

119
00:07:13,182 --> 00:07:15,475
There's no way you can
take on that many people!

120
00:07:15,476 --> 00:07:17,185
Let's get out of here
while we still can!

121
00:07:17,186 --> 00:07:20,188
Huh? You don't want me to die?

122
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:21,441
Ah...

123
00:07:23,359 --> 00:07:27,196
I don't want you to die! Never!

124
00:07:35,329 --> 00:07:36,622
Don't worry.

125
00:07:37,415 --> 00:07:39,917
I won't die.

126
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:43,171
Just wait here.
I'll be back in no time.

127
00:07:45,715 --> 00:07:47,175
Shinpei!

128
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:57,225
I never thought you'd actually
try to escape the island.

129
00:07:57,226 --> 00:08:00,729
You should've at least
said goodbye to me.

130
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:03,732
What? You were going to let me go?

131
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:06,194
I would've killed you
right where you stood.

132
00:08:08,404 --> 00:08:12,824
You lot! Don't let those two
leave this island alive!

133
00:08:12,825 --> 00:08:15,203
Get them!

134
00:08:43,356 --> 00:08:45,358
All brawn, no brains, huh?

135
00:08:55,159 --> 00:08:56,535
Don't falter...

136
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:58,119
I know...

137
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:01,541
But... that's not human.

138
00:09:03,417 --> 00:09:04,669
That's a demon.

139
00:09:05,419 --> 00:09:09,340
Hey, Goto! I'll get revenge
for you cutting off my left arm!

140
00:09:11,884 --> 00:09:13,427
Who are you again?

141
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:21,685
Stand down, Mr. Mitsueda.

142
00:09:21,686 --> 00:09:25,690
If you lose any more men,
you won't have anyone left to do the job.

143
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:32,655
I haven't lost anyone.

144
00:09:38,661 --> 00:09:41,247
<i>He hasn't killed a single one of them...</i>

145
00:09:42,164 --> 00:09:45,543
<i>No matter who they are,
you must never kill anyone!</i>

146
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:50,171
<i>Could it be because of
what I said back then?</i>

147
00:09:50,172 --> 00:09:52,591
Come on, you're not acting like yourself.

148
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:55,010
What the hell happened to you?

149
00:09:55,011 --> 00:09:58,513
Have you really been tamed by a woman?

150
00:09:58,514 --> 00:10:01,933
Come back to your senses, Goto.

151
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:04,562
There's no reason for you to die.

152
00:10:07,315 --> 00:10:08,983
Ah! Hey!

153
00:10:09,525 --> 00:10:10,901
Let go of me!

154
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:16,656
You've caused us enough trouble!

155
00:10:16,657 --> 00:10:17,992
Stay still!

156
00:10:23,831 --> 00:10:26,500
Shinpei! Now's our chance!
Let's flee!

157
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:53,026
Shinpei!

158
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:55,821
Are you all right?!

159
00:11:00,618 --> 00:11:02,286
{\an8}Don't touch her!

160
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:11,128
Shinpei! Shinpei!

161
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:13,255
Shinpei!

162
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:15,674
S...

163
00:11:16,967 --> 00:11:19,303
Satoko...

164
00:11:21,305 --> 00:11:22,390
Yes...

165
00:11:23,974 --> 00:11:25,184
I'll...

166
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:30,523
...give you my heart...

167
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:50,668
Shinpei!

168
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:52,086
Get off of him!

169
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:57,091
Get your foot off him!

170
00:12:02,263 --> 00:12:03,806
Get off!

171
00:12:04,932 --> 00:12:06,308
Get off him!

172
00:12:09,395 --> 00:12:11,105
That's enough, Shido.

173
00:12:12,523 --> 00:12:15,608
Shinpei! Shinpei!

174
00:12:15,609 --> 00:12:17,610
What's the matter, little lady?

175
00:12:17,611 --> 00:12:19,989
Why do you care if he dies?

176
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:25,911
He's already done for.

177
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:30,916
I'll put him out of his misery
and finish him off right now.

178
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:57,860
That bastard! They got away!

179
00:12:58,569 --> 00:13:01,779
It's fine. He won't survive
those wounds anyway.

180
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:04,824
But, boss! His vitality is far beyond
that of an ordinary man...

181
00:13:04,825 --> 00:13:06,535
I said it's fine.

182
00:13:07,703 --> 00:13:09,330
Just leave them.

183
00:13:24,553 --> 00:13:26,972
Shinpei! Shinpei!

184
00:13:33,062 --> 00:13:34,480
<i>No way...</i>

185
00:13:35,064 --> 00:13:36,564
<i>Could he already be...</i>

186
00:13:36,565 --> 00:13:39,150
<i>No, calm down...</i>

187
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:41,611
<i>It's okay... He'll be okay...</i>

188
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:44,239
<i>I need to get
the water out of his lungs.</i>

189
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:48,077
<i>The doctor told me
how to do that...</i>

190
00:13:54,833 --> 00:13:57,461
<i>Please... Open your eyes.</i>

191
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:02,633
Shinpei!

192
00:14:06,595 --> 00:14:08,055
<i>Stop!</i>

193
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:12,141
<i>Stop! Stop! Stop!</i>

194
00:14:12,142 --> 00:14:13,351
Satoko!

195
00:14:13,352 --> 00:14:14,353
Huh?

196
00:14:16,647 --> 00:14:17,815
Aoi?

197
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:21,235
{\an8}(Isekichi)

198
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:23,736
This is terrible.

199
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:26,739
The wound on his back is quite deep.

200
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:28,575
Fortunately, the wound in his abdomen

201
00:14:28,576 --> 00:14:30,660
doesn't seem to have
damaged any internal organs.

202
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:34,748
But several of his bones are shattered.
It's a miracle he's still alive.

203
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:39,503
Honestly, how did this happen?

204
00:14:44,842 --> 00:14:46,801
His body temperature is dangerously low.

205
00:14:46,802 --> 00:14:50,097
At this rate, there's a high
chance he won't survive.

206
00:14:53,434 --> 00:14:55,311
I'll come back to check on him later.

207
00:14:57,021 --> 00:14:58,771
What are you all doing here?!

208
00:14:58,772 --> 00:15:00,440
Get back to work!

209
00:15:00,441 --> 00:15:02,109
Satoko...

210
00:15:02,484 --> 00:15:03,611
Aoi...

211
00:15:04,403 --> 00:15:07,363
Thank you so much
for coming to our rescue.

212
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:11,493
Not at all. I just felt a little sad,
so I thought I'd come see you off.

213
00:15:17,207 --> 00:15:19,834
Have faith, Satoko.

214
00:15:19,835 --> 00:15:22,712
Mr. Shinpei will surely be all right.

215
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:26,926
He suffered a serious injury once before,
but recovered unbelievably quickly...

216
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:56,329
{\an8}Hey, newbie!

217
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,832
Has Mr. Shinpei woken up yet?

218
00:16:03,212 --> 00:16:05,296
No, not yet...

219
00:16:05,297 --> 00:16:08,217
It's already been seven days.
How is he?

220
00:16:08,801 --> 00:16:10,052
No change.

221
00:16:10,594 --> 00:16:12,637
I'll take over keeping watch.

222
00:16:12,638 --> 00:16:15,056
Why don't you take a nap in the meantime?

223
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:17,893
I'm more capable than you, after all.

224
00:16:19,687 --> 00:16:21,814
{\an8}Thank you for your concern.

225
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:24,274
But I'd like to stay by his side.

226
00:16:27,569 --> 00:16:29,195
Look at her face...

227
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:31,823
You'd think she was
the one on her deathbed.

228
00:16:31,824 --> 00:16:34,033
Honestly, what a dull woman.

229
00:16:34,034 --> 00:16:36,453
Can't she even show a little emotion?

230
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:40,082
Sometimes,
there's just no saving someone.

231
00:16:40,582 --> 00:16:42,501
Humans are fragile creatures.

232
00:17:34,344 --> 00:17:38,598
<i>We'll be able to leave
this island safely by boat!</i>

233
00:17:38,599 --> 00:17:39,599
<i>That's it!</i>

234
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:43,895
<i>Once we get off this island, let's build
a house where fireflies appear every year.</i>

235
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:47,231
<i>That hurt. I'm bleeding.</i>

236
00:17:47,232 --> 00:17:51,194
<i>Compared to mine,
your scar is nothing at all.</i>

237
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:54,448
<i>My heart belongs to you, Satoko.</i>

238
00:17:55,032 --> 00:17:56,950
<i>I won't die.</i>

239
00:17:57,451 --> 00:18:00,079
<i>It's my job to protect you.</i>

240
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:05,250
<i>I'll set you free no matter
where we are, Satoko.</i>

241
00:18:52,923 --> 00:18:54,133
Is this heaven?

242
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:05,936
Satoko...

243
00:19:08,939 --> 00:19:09,939
Are you hurt?

244
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:12,859
Don't get up yet!
I'm fine!

245
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:14,570
Wait, I'll get someone right...

246
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:21,743
I'm sorry.
I'll do better next time.

247
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:28,125
One side of my body
felt warm the whole time.

248
00:19:29,209 --> 00:19:32,129
So you've been
keeping me warm all this time.

249
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:34,381
I'm happy.

250
00:19:35,215 --> 00:19:38,135
If you'd stayed by my side like that,

251
00:19:38,635 --> 00:19:41,263
maybe dying back then
wouldn't have been so bad.

252
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:50,022
Sorry, what did you just say?

253
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:54,359
I don't want your heart!

254
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:58,863
What do you mean, dying back then
wouldn't have been so bad?!

255
00:19:58,864 --> 00:20:04,119
I hate those ominous jokes of yours!

256
00:20:13,629 --> 00:20:16,715
You promised you wouldn't die,

257
00:20:17,174 --> 00:20:19,300
so I believed you...

258
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:22,012
Everyone said you might
never wake up again...

259
00:20:22,638 --> 00:20:26,099
I was so scared...

260
00:20:41,865 --> 00:20:46,078
W-Wait, Shinpei!
What are you...

261
00:20:47,955 --> 00:20:50,332
Please stop this!

262
00:20:51,124 --> 00:20:54,086
I beg you, Shinpei...

263
00:21:01,843 --> 00:21:05,555
Eek!

264
00:21:06,473 --> 00:21:09,309
What's wrong?!
Did something happen to Mr. Shinpei?!

265
00:21:11,895 --> 00:21:13,563
This is...

266
00:21:14,606 --> 00:21:16,732
Oh, he seems fine.

267
00:21:16,733 --> 00:21:20,069
Y-You...

268
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:23,365
You sly vixen!

269
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:34,418
<i>I could live on even alone</i>

270
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:38,672
<i>So I never feared anything</i>

271
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:42,675
<i>No matter what, no matter what</i>

272
00:21:42,676 --> 00:21:50,350
<i>My mind was filled
with nothing but questions</i>

273
00:21:51,101 --> 00:21:57,023
<i>More than anything, I was just afraid</i>

274
00:21:57,024 --> 00:22:00,902
{\an8}<i>Of losing your warm skin</i>

275
00:22:02,487 --> 00:22:08,242
<i>As if our sorrows were blending
together, just the two of us</i>

276
00:22:08,243 --> 00:22:12,831
<i>No matter where we go,
please don't let me go</i>

277
00:22:13,790 --> 00:22:19,462
<i>Let's comfort each other
as many times as we have wounds</i>

278
00:22:19,463 --> 00:22:25,468
<i>Even if it means burning
our lives away until death</i>

279
00:22:25,469 --> 00:22:29,347
<i>I believe that will never change</i>

280
00:22:30,223 --> 00:22:35,478
<i>In my arms,
the ones everyone feared</i>

281
00:22:35,479 --> 00:22:41,233
<i>The one who cried
in them, my beloved</i>

282
00:22:41,234 --> 00:22:46,822
{\an8}<i>I could live on even alone</i>

283
00:22:46,823 --> 00:22:51,952
<i>So I never feared anything</i>

284
00:22:51,953 --> 00:22:54,122
<i>But I did</i>

